## What Each Engine Does & The Researched Math

### ENGINE 5 — Pose Comparison Engine

**Job:** Compute the physical differences between the target and user pose.
**Output:** The `Pose Error Model`.

```dart
// The Pose Error Model is a map of these objects:
class JointError {
  final PoseLandmarkType joint;
  final double dx;               // target.x - user.x (normalized)
  final double dy;               // target.y - user.y (normalized)
  final double distance;         // √(dx² + dy²)
  final double confidence;       // ML Kit visibility
  final int frameIndex;          // Monotonic frame counter (NOT epoch time)
                                 // Camera pipelines don't guarantee stable wall-clock time.
                                 // Use frame index for velocity, EMA, and temporal logic.
  final ErrorType errorType;     // What kind of mistake this is
  
  // Future-proofing (Engine 5 computes, Engine 6 decides)
  final double? angleError;
  final double? rotationError;
  final double? visibility;
  final double? weight;
}

enum ErrorType {
  translation,   // Joint is in the wrong position (dx/dy)
  rotation,      // Joint is rotated wrong (future: angleError)
  scale,         // Limb length mismatch
  visibility,    // ML Kit can't see this joint clearly
  symmetry,      // Left/right body asymmetry
}
```

